Even if an organization doesn't have a specific policy regarding usenet
postings, it's not much of a stretch to invoke restrictions of the carrying
network if necessary.  Many universities, for example, have news traffic
flowing by way of NFSNET, which has a reasonably clear acceptable use policy.
Junk postings on usenet don't seem to be covered by that policy.  The various
regional nets have similar policies.  In fact, since virtually all news
eventually finds its way through every network imaginable, any number of
acceptable use policies could be violated by certain categories of postings.
