Date: Tue, 23 Feb 1993 23:34:40 GMT

In my Gopher server [gopher.lysator.liu.se 70] I have links to some
local MUD games (type 8 entries, access by telnet).  It seems from
gopher log file statistics that this is quite popular.

I have received a letter suggesting that I should remove this option,
because a Gopher should be serious and games are not serious.
Moreover, my Gopher service had been accessed through an anonymous
gopher account where users were not supposed to play games.

I denied this suggestion on the grounds that my service only provided
the information needed to connect to the game (hostname and port),
which is public anyway, and that the type 8 connect option should be
removed at the anonymous client.  We did not agree on this.

I'd like to hear from other Gopher admins, what similar experience
they have had, and from all, what you think about games and gophers.
